<div>
    <div id=3D"macroeconomic-shifts" class=3D"cmp-text ">
        <p><i>How could the macroeconomic realities in 2026 impact the bank=
ing and capital markets industry=E2=80=99s revenues and profitability?</i><=
/p>
<p><i>What does the disruptive entrance of stablecoins mean for banks and p=
ayment firms?</i></p>
<p><i>What should banks do in 2026 to industrialize AI at scale?</i></p>
<p><i>Will some banks=E2=80=99 AI ambitions be thwarted by their brittle an=
d fragmented data infrastructure?</i></p>
<p><i>Can banks=E2=80=99 defenses keep up with the increasing speed and sop=
histication of financial crime?</i></p>

    </div>
</div>

   =20

</div>
<div class=3D"text cmp-di-text pr-0 pl-0 pl-mob-2 pr-mob-2 aem-GridColumn--=
phone--12 cmp-di-text--line-height-large aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--def=
ault--12">

   =20

<div class=3D"hide-no-results-error-msg">
    <img src=3D"https://www.deloitte.com/content/dam/insights/icons/svg/ico=
n-alert.svg"> =20
</div>
<div>
    <div class=3D"cmp-text ">
        <p>2026 appears to be shaping up as a defining year for US banks. M=
acroeconomic uncertainty, diverging consumer sentiment, and persistent infl=
ation could test banks=E2=80=99 revenues and profitability, even as strong =
capital positions provide resilience. Banks could be forced to defend margi=
ns, diversify fee income, and prepare for increased competition from nonban=
k entities.</p>
<p>The payments landscape also seems to be at a crossroads. Stablecoins, ba=
cked by the new Guiding and Establishing National Innovation for US Stablec=
oins Act legislation, could impact deposit flows and challenge traditional =
payment rails. Banks should decide whether to issue, custody, process, or p=
artner=E2=80=94and do so quickly, as tokenized deposits and programmable mo=
ney reshape customer expectations.</p>

    </div>
</div>

